.TH WIFI-HOTSPOT-SETTINGS 1 "" "RelayForge" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wifi-hotspot-settings \- configure RelayForge Wi-Fi sharing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wifi-hotspot-settings
.RB [ --standalone | --about ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens the GTK settings editor, or an integrated GNOME Wi-Fi panel when its
RelayForge integration marker is installed. Run as the desktop user.
Sharing and protected configuration changes require service authorization.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --standalone
Open the editor directly, including when GNOME integration is available.
.TP
.B --about
Show RelayForge version, project links and component credits without reading
protected configuration or contacting the hotspot service.
.SH OPTIONAL CONTROLS
The relayforge-tray companion provides wifi-hotspot-tray. Launching it explicitly
shows the icon. Login startup honors saved startup and visibility preferences.
Quit stops sharing before exiting; closing the settings editor leaves sharing
running. A desktop with AppIndicator support is required for the tray icon.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/wifi-hotspot.conf
is an explicitly initialized administrator-owned configuration.
Per-user desktop preferences are retained on package removal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR relayforge-service (8)
